    "text": "Ester containing <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> -hydrogens undergo self condensation in presence of a strong base such as sodium ethoxide to form <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> -ketoesters. This reaction is called Claisen condensation.<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow></mover></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mover><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"false\"><mo>→</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mover><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo>|</mo></mrow></mover></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mtext>-keto&nbsp;ester</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math><br /><br />Crossed-Claisen condensation is feasible only when one of the reactants has no <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> -hydrogen and is thus incapable of undergoing self condensation. For example<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/12_soud_ched.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 59px;\" />",
